{#
  Render env_vars_report_entries for one host as plain text lines.

  Layout mechanics (column-0 block tags, plain ASCII, why not colour) are
  the same as the other reports' templates - see
  roles/toolchain_report/templates/toolchain-report.j2 for the rationale.

  Grouped by managed block because that is the unit an operator acts on: a
  host may carry several consumers' blocks in one file, and the block name
  is what says which declaration produced a line and which one to go and
  edit. The status column repeats inside a group - it is a property of the
  block, so every row of a group carries the same value - and it is
  printed per row anyway so that a group read in isolation is still
  complete, and so the two reports' rows read alike.

  The file each block lives in is on the GROUP heading rather than on each
  row: it is one fact per block, and repeating it per variable would push
  the value - the thing an operator came to read - off to the right. It is
  taken as the distinct set of the group's targets rather than as the
  first row's, so a group whose rows ever disagreed says so instead of
  quietly reporting one of them.

  Values are printed in single quotes, which the file's own NAME="value"
  lines never use. Two reasons, both about not misleading: the value here
  is the DECLARED one, so a double-quoted rendering would invite an
  operator to read the escaping off a line that carries none; and the
  quotes are what make surrounding whitespace visible, which is otherwise
  the one kind of wrong value a report can print indistinguishably from
  the right one.

  The header counts statuses only, like every sibling report. A total
  would be the sum of the two numbers beside it.

  Ordering is stable without sorting anything here: groupby sorts by the
  grouping key, and within a group the rows keep accumulator order - which
  is the order the variables were declared in, so a group can be read
  against the config it came from line by line.
#}
{% set entries = env_vars_report_entries | default([]) %}
{% set written = entries | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'written') | list %}
{% set unchanged = entries | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'unchanged') | list %}
Environment variables report for {{ inventory_hostname }} -- {{ written | length }} written, {{ unchanged | length }} unchanged
{% if not entries %}
  (no environment variables were declared - nothing was written here)
{% endif %}
{% for block, rows in entries | groupby('block') %}
  block {{ block }} -- {{ rows | length }} declared in {{ rows | map(attribute='target') | unique | join(', ') }}
{% for entry in rows %}
    {{ "%-9s" | format(entry.status) }} {{ entry.name }}='{{ entry.value }}'
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
